# 37. Definition of Done

Phase 2 is complete when all of the following are true:

* [ ] SQLite database is created successfully.
* [ ] Experience records can be stored.
* [ ] `nomic-embed-text` generates embeddings.
* [ ] sqlite-vec stores embeddings.
* [ ] Semantic similarity search works.
* [ ] Top-K memory retrieval works.
* [ ] Similarity threshold works.
* [ ] Retrieved memories are supplied to the LLM.
* [ ] New experiences are persisted.
* [ ] Memory survives application/session restart.
* [ ] Agent continues working when no memory exists.
* [ ] ADK Web remains the only agent/chat interface.
* [ ] Streamlit developer application works.
* [ ] Streamlit can inspect SQLite tables.
* [ ] Streamlit can inspect experiences.
* [ ] Streamlit can inspect vector information.
* [ ] Streamlit can perform semantic search.
* [ ] Streamlit can show similarity results.
* [ ] Streamlit is read-only.
* [ ] Logging shows the memory retrieval flow.
* [ ] Automated tests pass.
* [ ] README is updated.
* [ ] No self-evaluation or self-learning functionality has been introduced.

---

# 38. Phase 2 Success Statement

At the end of Phase 2, the system should demonstrate:

> **"The agent can remember previous experiences, find relevant memories using semantic vector search, use those memories while answering new requests, persist the memories in SQLite, and allow the developer to visually inspect how the memory system works through Streamlit."**

This provides the foundation for **Phase 3 — Self-Evaluation, Learning, and Graph-Based Relationships**.
